@Adminiuga the problem is that the behavior is inconsistent with other integrations.

In ZHA, couldn't we prevent the level from being passed to the entity during the transition? For example, if ZHA receives a turn_off command with a transition, ZHA ignores every level change report until the light is off, or until it receives another command (that may cancel the turn_off command). This will work better than just waiting for X seconds, because that will bring timing issues.

When the turn_on service is sent again, ZHA should tell the light to turn on to the previous brightness (that would be stored in the entity).
